    <section>
      <p><small>What HireLens offers</small></p>
      <h1>Services</h1>
      <p>HireLens helps recruiters screen resumes faster and understand every result. Each service below works on the same idea: match resumes to a job description and show the reasons behind the score.</p>
    </section>

    <hr>

    <section>
      <h2>Our services</h2>

      <article>
        <h3>Explained scores</h3>
        <p>Every candidate gets a score out of 100 with a clear breakdown. You can see which keywords matched and which are missing, so you know why a candidate ranked where they did.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Weighted keyword matching</h3>
        <p>HireLens finds the skills the job asks for and checks them against each resume. Skills, experience, education and formatting each count towards the final score.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Synonym-aware matching</h3>
        <p>Different resumes use different words for the same skill. HireLens treats JS and JavaScript as the same skill, so good candidates are not missed.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Blind review mode</h3>
        <p>Hide names and contact details while ranking, so candidates are compared on their skills and experience.</p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h3>Candidate ranking</h3>
        <p>Upload a batch of resumes and get a ranked list, with the best matches at the top.</p>
      </article>
    </section>

